(A copy of a thing whose buffer field was freed holds an empty buffer of its
 own, which takes writes as any new buffer does: it was never freed. The
 original's field stays freed.)
A thing called note has
  a buffer called body.

a note called memo.
append "ab" to memo's body.
Free memo's body.
a note called copied is memo.
append "fresh" to copied's body.
On error print "the copy refused the append".
Print "copied: {copied's body}, size {copied's body's size}".
Print "memo: {memo's body's size}".
